course: dictionary
lesson: 3645
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary gives the main meaning first, then a second one, sometimes marked (informal) for everyday, chatty talk. To choose the right meaning, look at the context: the words and sentences around the word. «A firecracker going off in a hand can break bones and burn flesh.» Here a firecracker is clearly the small firework that explodes with a bang.
explain: The second meaning describes a person. Someone who is a firecracker is lively, energetic and quick to lose their temper. Read this: «Ruby is a real firecracker, always full of ideas and quick to flare up.» Flare up is the clue: people flare up, fireworks do not.
explain: Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: A firecracker is a small firework that explodes with a loud bang, often in a string of many.
fact: «A firecracker going off in a hand can break bones and burn flesh.» So never pick up a firecracker that did not go off.
fact: Only adults should light fireworks, and pets should be kept indoors when firecrackers are set off.
fact: «Fàng biānpào» is the Chinese phrase for setting off firecrackers, often at midnight in China and at parades in Chinatown.
fact: (informal) A firecracker can also be a lively, energetic, quick-tempered person.
exercise: «A firecracker going off in a hand can break bones and burn flesh.» What is a firecracker in this sentence? | A kind of cake | A lively, energetic person | *A small firework that explodes with a loud bang | A coloured light on a bridge
exercise: Ruby is a real firecracker, always full of energy and quick to lose her temper. What does firecracker mean here? | A small firework | A tool for cooking | A loud noise at midnight | *A lively, quick-tempered person
exercise: Which phrase means firecrackers joined together in a line? | *a string of firecrackers | a bunch of flowers | a sack of sweets | a bag of crackers
test: What should you do if you find a firecracker that did not go off? | Put it in your pocket to keep it safe | Pick it up quickly and throw it away | *Leave it alone and tell an adult | Light it again to check it
test: Which is the best safety rule for firecrackers? | Children should light them in the garden alone | Pets should be left outside to watch | Hold one in your hand to test it | *Only adults should light them
exam: Why should firecrackers never be thrown at people or houses? | They make the sky look prettier | They help the neighbours sleep better | They keep flies away from the house | *They can cause burns, fires and great fright
